"""Write THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt: the license and notice texts of everything a release ships.

tools/third-party-licenses.toml names the project and where its components come from: Rust crates
(cargo), Go modules, npm packages, Python packages, vendored files listed by hand, and the Arch
system libraries it links (listed for reference). Run it after any dependency change; `--check`
fails when the file no longer matches. It needs Python 3.11 and each ecosystem's own tool, reads
sources from their local caches, and so works offline once the project has been built.

Adapted from Flea's tools/flea-third-party-licenses, Copyright (c) 2026 GM, under the MIT License.
"""

